I have analyzed the Kaggle error log and successfully identified the root cause of the `FileNotFoundError`.

### 1. Root Cause Analysis
In Kaggle code competitions, the execution environment for hidden test sets sometimes mounts the competition dataset at a slightly different directory path (e.g., `/kaggle/input/competitions/stanford-rna-3d-folding-2` instead of the hardcoded `/kaggle/input/stanford-rna-3d-folding-2`). Because the notebook in `script_v37.py` had this directory hardcoded, the script crashed with a `FileNotFoundError` when attempting to load `test_sequences.csv`.

### 2. Fix Implementation
I created `notebooks/script_v38.py` from `script_v37.py` and implemented a dynamic filesystem search (using `pathlib.Path('/kaggle/input').rglob(...)`) to locate `test_sequences.csv` and the other necessary dataset files on the fly. This fallback ensures the files are always found regardless of the specific Kaggle mount point.

### 3. Summary
