I have debugged the issue and applied the fix to `notebooks/script_v47.py`.

### Root Cause
The `papermill` execution encountered a `FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/kaggle/input/stanford-rna-3d-folding-2/test_sequences.csv'`. This happened because the dataset path was hardcoded. Kaggle's hidden test set often alters directory structures or mounts inputs slightly differently.

### Fix
I restored the dynamic path resolution logic (using `Path("/kaggle/input").rglob()`) previously used in `v38` to locate `test_sequences.csv` dynamically rather than relying on a static string, avoiding the `FileNotFoundError`.

I have also updated `current_strategy.txt` with a 1-line summary of the change.
